[{:db/id "q-114699/selection/1c4fcd04f2c50fe2c4eaeac6025140665ca0e7e7cfaa5117d3979d44e4b8d848" :answer/id #uuid "5cd81f6f-884d-5823-babd-7a97e30ab1c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{8}(-4{x}^{2}+2x+3)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114699/selection/cff3bd09df5c5b5c194b0ed9b5be28337c4491c9c5944fb1ba7498012824c1ff" :answer/id #uuid "5f78642a-97ed-5667-afeb-0bd4e1307d7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}(4{x}^{2}-2x+1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114699/selection/7fa190ed00c69d451f0066ae3f170066c8d063be418277f6168e3ae1f813c733" :answer/id #uuid "8cac9766-9aa7-58f8-95fd-3dfac5f607d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-8{x}^{2}+4x+3)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114699/selection/899bdb4a2fd41968ce8c99a969a42297c8fb27631e3a092832feb21f5c822400" :answer/id #uuid "c5933fc9-eef9-52da-a8ec-7f90a069326e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-4{x}^{2}+2x+1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114699/selection/4779fc8a1932cbf34f968a5cd281b003a1ecbabf2e02a4c8e987ebe90933bf4a" :answer/id #uuid "fb5559a1-7a4f-5bcd-a4d5-b3ae9abc9c55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{8}(2{x}^{2}+x+4)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114699/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "04330c49-8b20-59c5-9c58-146f02e226f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114699/selection/7fa190ed00c69d451f0066ae3f170066c8d063be418277f6168e3ae1f813c733" :answer-field/choices ["q-114699/selection/1c4fcd04f2c50fe2c4eaeac6025140665ca0e7e7cfaa5117d3979d44e4b8d848" "q-114699/selection/cff3bd09df5c5b5c194b0ed9b5be28337c4491c9c5944fb1ba7498012824c1ff" "q-114699/selection/7fa190ed00c69d451f0066ae3f170066c8d063be418277f6168e3ae1f813c733" "q-114699/selection/899bdb4a2fd41968ce8c99a969a42297c8fb27631e3a092832feb21f5c822400" "q-114699/selection/4779fc8a1932cbf34f968a5cd281b003a1ecbabf2e02a4c8e987ebe90933bf4a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114699" :question/id #uuid "2c9066df-83e6-5801-b1b9-4c9e71b9624d" :question/math-academy-id "q-114699" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int (1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=1-2{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(1-2{x}^{2})(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4})(-4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}}{4}+\\int x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{4x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{4})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{4}-\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(4x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}}{4}+(\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(4x-1)+C) \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2}){e}^{4x}}{4}+\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(4x-1)+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{16}(-8{x}^{2}+4x+3)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114699/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b69f026a-50b3-505d-bd9d-8b295691b66e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114699"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352110/field-1/39e3d7270bcd5393015644f396c7db64d6d9ab879ce5bdb2e877e68843c765a5" :answer/id #uuid "650eabd9-5b5d-512a-81a6-cd58c4ae5ccc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{11e^4-11e^2}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352110/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "9189c499-b8c7-5b54-b5f4-ccf6cdfcc58f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352110/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "80bfeab6-b03f-5a2a-a2ed-a9d231928089" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352110/field-1/39e3d7270bcd5393015644f396c7db64d6d9ab879ce5bdb2e877e68843c765a5" :answer-field/choices ["q-352110/field-1/39e3d7270bcd5393015644f396c7db64d6d9ab879ce5bdb2e877e68843c765a5" "q-352110/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352110" :question/id #uuid "0b08a740-f9cc-5206-9af4-09998ba57a3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-352110" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={x}^{2}+5\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{2x+2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2}+5)(\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2})(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\int x\\,{e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x\\,{e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{2x+2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\,{e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x)(\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{2})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\,{e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\,{e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\int x\\,{e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}}{2}-(\\frac{x\\,{e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}}{2}-\\frac{x\\,{e}^{2x+2}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}-D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}(2{x}^{2}-2x+11)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-D.$ \n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+5){e}^{2x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{e}^{2x+2}}{4}(2{x}^{2}-2x+11)]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{2(1)+2}}{4}(2(1)^{2}-2(1)+11))-(\\frac{{e}^{2(0)+2}}{4}(2(0)^{2}-2(0)+11)) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4}}{4}(2-2+11)-\\frac{{e}^{2}}{4}(0-0+11) \\\\  & =\\frac{11{e}^{4}}{4}-\\frac{11{e}^{2}}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{11{e}^{4}-11{e}^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352110/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b69f026a-50b3-505d-bd9d-8b295691b66e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352110"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-12703/selection/3853cc59f58d0864468183caf1314e1bb74c8d8af7fca77b89dc8e5c0c4bd8ba" :answer/id #uuid "f5377a1d-ac49-5187-abed-b84aba987c4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{e}^{3x}}{27}(9{x}^{2}-6x+2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12703/selection/ceb94a4d32ef2f7897ff7d35a98d9e960d8ab58c0adcc3ff41b334f291c18f9e" :answer/id #uuid "8bbd35d8-9e10-51a9-9707-7e3f7c755a75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{e}^{3x}}{27}(3{x}^{2}-2x+1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12703/selection/1666201cf5cb4eb86a92047cc1d8cfa446fd4ebd008352046a6565bdb8ee8498" :answer/id #uuid "1dc0986f-1377-5e85-9126-d02215dbff9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{e}^{3x}}{9}(6{x}^{2}-3x+1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12703/selection/8dbfbbfc499795c86a36067ad51b017a828aa938a2e9faf7bdbcb343e3eda1f6" :answer/id #uuid "1fc4cd22-46a2-5171-ae3f-601aa6a83bcb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{e}^{3x}}{9}(3{x}^{2}+6x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12703/selection/b6921245184585bbd91cbfb80b5235859819e4dc1a76a01227e7d39d4b04c0be" :answer/id #uuid "24af7bd0-3594-5184-a675-092a73990907" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{e}^{3x}}{27}(3{x}^{2}+3x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12703/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "50046095-1f57-5762-a89f-7d0ca42bb462" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-12703/selection/3853cc59f58d0864468183caf1314e1bb74c8d8af7fca77b89dc8e5c0c4bd8ba" :answer-field/choices ["q-12703/selection/3853cc59f58d0864468183caf1314e1bb74c8d8af7fca77b89dc8e5c0c4bd8ba" "q-12703/selection/ceb94a4d32ef2f7897ff7d35a98d9e960d8ab58c0adcc3ff41b334f291c18f9e" "q-12703/selection/1666201cf5cb4eb86a92047cc1d8cfa446fd4ebd008352046a6565bdb8ee8498" "q-12703/selection/8dbfbbfc499795c86a36067ad51b017a828aa938a2e9faf7bdbcb343e3eda1f6" "q-12703/selection/b6921245184585bbd91cbfb80b5235859819e4dc1a76a01227e7d39d4b04c0be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-12703" :question/id #uuid "d0a75ed6-0047-57b5-9fef-0aefe85b4f47" :question/math-academy-id "q-12703" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 5{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=10x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(5{x}^{2})(\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})(10x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}\\int x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{3x}\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}+D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}(3x-1)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 5{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{5{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{10}{3}(\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}(3x-1)+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{2}{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{10{e}^{3x}}{27}(3x-1)-\\frac{10D}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3x}}{27}(9{x}^{2}-6x+2)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{10D}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-12703/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b69f026a-50b3-505d-bd9d-8b295691b66e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-12703"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-351977/field-1/355dc1ab5613cfd562b4c73fdf7f9c8402891189e0d8c1977666fdd9adb1ca64" :answer/id #uuid "af518ab5-8ee9-5038-8f1a-841e13957e5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5e^4-1}{32}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351977/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "f8139e4c-20fe-5454-95be-82a9279d118c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-351977/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d73185ed-9801-5fed-91e8-f0eaee340ae1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-351977/field-1/355dc1ab5613cfd562b4c73fdf7f9c8402891189e0d8c1977666fdd9adb1ca64" :answer-field/choices ["q-351977/field-1/355dc1ab5613cfd562b4c73fdf7f9c8402891189e0d8c1977666fdd9adb1ca64" "q-351977/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-351977" :question/id #uuid "987eb95b-655e-5f6f-b8ef-5120b686db4e" :question/math-academy-id "q-351977" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={t}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2t, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{4t}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {t}^{2}{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({t}^{2})(\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4t})-\\int (\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4t})(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int t{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int t{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=1, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{4t}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int t{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t)(\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4t})-\\int (\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4t})(1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}t{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{4}\\int {e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}t{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{16}{e}^{4t}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {t}^{2}{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int t{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{4}t{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{16}{e}^{4t}+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{8}t{e}^{4t}+\\frac{1}{32}{e}^{4t}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{D}{2}.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}\\,\\text{d}t & =(\\frac{1}{4}{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}-\\frac{1}{8}t{e}^{4t}+\\frac{1}{32}{e}^{4t})\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}({1}^{2}){e}^{4}-\\frac{1}{8}(1){e}^{4}+\\frac{1}{32}{e}^{4})-(\\frac{1}{4}({0}^{2}){e}^{0}-\\frac{1}{8}(0){e}^{0}+\\frac{1}{32}{e}^{0}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{32}{e}^{4}-\\frac{1}{32} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{4}-1}{32}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-351977/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b69f026a-50b3-505d-bd9d-8b295691b66e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-351977"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114695/selection/a22e3440845f611c74e2d679a8db3e4e836afa47baaaa0ce4a8cd4680da895ae" :answer/id #uuid "76c6c241-09d2-51ca-b990-23bc1cfb96f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}({x}^{2}-x+1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114695/selection/230327ef540e0c55ff58fbf309740f06d0012f6b82d811638e39f05e3e0fc518" :answer/id #uuid "95b660dc-f57e-5487-81b2-f3803a0240da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}(3{x}^{2}-x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114695/selection/f6c45c61a34f1da850e066224929bbae1cca6c40f60cf8d5ffd864ef41979e73" :answer/id #uuid "4c00a34d-f412-56c5-9350-ef39ccb72b29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}(2{x}^{2}-x+2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114695/selection/a05400c840231073e5d625639073db038c2f757ec67a3990c685f8ca9972bddf" :answer/id #uuid "ffa8622f-fee1-51f4-943d-7a8b2dcc4b72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}({x}^{2}-2x-2)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114695/selection/3e193b0e78298894eedac01a717dd7e1b0af4dc73afcd4aa942ffe95ad3d924a" :answer/id #uuid "2a8d337d-33a4-5799-a422-a4667d8b8bc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{e}^{x}(4{x}^{2}-4x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114695/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9b23390-7bc3-5318-9297-e4d46ef5d74c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114695/selection/a05400c840231073e5d625639073db038c2f757ec67a3990c685f8ca9972bddf" :answer-field/choices ["q-114695/selection/a22e3440845f611c74e2d679a8db3e4e836afa47baaaa0ce4a8cd4680da895ae" "q-114695/selection/230327ef540e0c55ff58fbf309740f06d0012f6b82d811638e39f05e3e0fc518" "q-114695/selection/f6c45c61a34f1da850e066224929bbae1cca6c40f60cf8d5ffd864ef41979e73" "q-114695/selection/a05400c840231073e5d625639073db038c2f757ec67a3990c685f8ca9972bddf" "q-114695/selection/3e193b0e78298894eedac01a717dd7e1b0af4dc73afcd4aa942ffe95ad3d924a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114695" :question/id #uuid "544a1f7e-f2b4-5338-9e60-b5044f7f7a8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-114695" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int ({x}^{2}-4){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={x}^{2}-4\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x={e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}-4){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-4)({e}^{x})-\\int ({e}^{x})(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-4){e}^{x}-2\\int x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x={e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x({e}^{x})-\\int ({e}^{x})(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{e}^{x}-\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{e}^{x}-{e}^{x}+D \\\\  & ={e}^{x}(x-1)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({x}^{2}-4){e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =({x}^{2}-4){e}^{x}-2({e}^{x}(x-1)+D) \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-4){e}^{x}-2(x-1){e}^{x}-2D \\\\  & ={e}^{x}({x}^{2}-2x-2)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-2D.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-114695/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b69f026a-50b3-505d-bd9d-8b295691b66e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114695"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352030/field-1/28aa9135c9538c36303f0f7b8ba20e87a845a6156a59161566447dd6e3760739" :answer/id #uuid "1ddaad8d-34f6-54fd-9bc1-ea1b1be17c8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{4}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352030/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "627aceca-f6da-50c8-a1e4-cb20dca9e289" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352030/field-1/28aa9135c9538c36303f0f7b8ba20e87a845a6156a59161566447dd6e3760739" :answer-field/choices ["q-352030/field-1/28aa9135c9538c36303f0f7b8ba20e87a845a6156a59161566447dd6e3760739"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352030" :question/id #uuid "51c18efa-0007-538d-9f04-b86c4f705e59" :question/math-academy-id "q-352030" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2})(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2})\\cdot 1\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2(\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{4}+D) \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2D.$\n\nFinally, then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(-{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )+(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )}{2}) \\\\  & \\,-(-(0)^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)}{2}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{1}{2})-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352030/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2a41ede-381e-55f6-99e5-1baf1ea348a1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352030"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352118/field-1/67d5446e8210d01b40a4882d59aa354216dd7cb5dc62eb7885dc189beb11172f" :answer/id #uuid "9e9cc958-7512-517d-b52c-aea07d8ec9fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6\\pi" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352118/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "38512790-608a-5e6b-a200-5aab0f30a666" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352118/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f1e216c-c280-5d3e-aa68-471a4a140fdc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352118/field-1/67d5446e8210d01b40a4882d59aa354216dd7cb5dc62eb7885dc189beb11172f" :answer-field/choices ["q-352118/field-1/67d5446e8210d01b40a4882d59aa354216dd7cb5dc62eb7885dc189beb11172f" "q-352118/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352118" :question/id #uuid "b5643990-8efc-5e32-9780-b8086ee0082b" :question/math-academy-id "q-352118" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x) & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x))\\cdot 1\\,dx \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,dx \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-6(-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+D) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-6D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={[3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)+6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(3(\\pi )^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+6(\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi ))-(3(0)^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+6(0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-6\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =0+6\\pi (-1)-0-0 \\\\  & =-6\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352118/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2a41ede-381e-55f6-99e5-1baf1ea348a1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352118"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-50233/selection/a1e2df77eb777abd1e7eaa46faab831ebd6a54e5ace5497fddaf36692cc5aa65" :answer/id #uuid "e92c7e7f-0898-5495-8775-9f89571247a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2{x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50233/selection/ef1cd57555a3ebf47378117927e1619d336f651ef2a80e702bf4f296f2b456f5" :answer/id #uuid "62528880-3824-52d7-9490-8fbbb6b80665" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({x}^{2}-1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50233/selection/f252f4979fff06da61f0404994342cc4e1deee432340f3e55c23f04ea232f75b" :answer/id #uuid "f2e4cb19-bf65-5cb1-8c71-b34b73c822fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({x}^{2}-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50233/selection/f1876e0d0d445a045940ba49c7fcb322a9359180b496230ee74e221d5233e76e" :answer/id #uuid "67618cd1-4594-5970-b16d-00e36b209fab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "({x}^{2}+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50233/selection/ef063d6518434717aec9258d7ed0fa26e0895b7924cb51de4c270c94184c78e0" :answer/id #uuid "eddb82aa-4fdb-5efb-ae9a-998c74423330" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50233/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f675360-100a-535b-a981-36590c8d2cec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-50233/selection/f252f4979fff06da61f0404994342cc4e1deee432340f3e55c23f04ea232f75b" :answer-field/choices ["q-50233/selection/a1e2df77eb777abd1e7eaa46faab831ebd6a54e5ace5497fddaf36692cc5aa65" "q-50233/selection/ef1cd57555a3ebf47378117927e1619d336f651ef2a80e702bf4f296f2b456f5" "q-50233/selection/f252f4979fff06da61f0404994342cc4e1deee432340f3e55c23f04ea232f75b" "q-50233/selection/f1876e0d0d445a045940ba49c7fcb322a9359180b496230ee74e221d5233e76e" "q-50233/selection/ef063d6518434717aec9258d7ed0fa26e0895b7924cb51de4c270c94184c78e0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-50233" :question/id #uuid "b6dd9b6b-3c69-5660-bb09-ed27bba9154f" :question/math-academy-id "q-50233" :question/problem "$\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1))-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)-2\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x)(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1))-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1))(1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)-2(-x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+D) \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)-2D \\\\  & =({x}^{2}-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-1)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-2D.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-50233/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2a41ede-381e-55f6-99e5-1baf1ea348a1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-50233"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-50222/selection/e585961168136308883bd18c8518e562356af440eb8894011e6bf5cdc4a06f6d" :answer/id #uuid "d117ffe3-c3d7-5eee-ae31-b5b703cd18d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50222/selection/97d71fe5c5f921b5356963390acbe0a4c5f8cc2fe6963586291a8eb59f62b9b8" :answer/id #uuid "2d5b3f94-5e85-5322-abb5-034e8f7d8372" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50222/selection/f2bba68d882be7460056eb5912844719ada485c852eee90d04d7481a6bdf5ffc" :answer/id #uuid "b0547144-d893-58da-af99-1ef6b0308476" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50222/selection/c8d82fdc73de0541a9c808403f76f7917b4b2dd9eff2e49dd7c7822a871dd384" :answer/id #uuid "a8ec805b-820f-55b0-a01e-d13461e7dccb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{2}+\\frac{3}{2}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50222/selection/58e3c9399a29c5a879685076ec2d3300653449b0f341bd390570fbd0f6a03961" :answer/id #uuid "00a9b071-3eb0-5171-9e71-fb71052b1031" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-50222/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "34ea7374-e58c-515b-af1a-7c1970f023c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-50222/selection/58e3c9399a29c5a879685076ec2d3300653449b0f341bd390570fbd0f6a03961" :answer-field/choices ["q-50222/selection/e585961168136308883bd18c8518e562356af440eb8894011e6bf5cdc4a06f6d" "q-50222/selection/97d71fe5c5f921b5356963390acbe0a4c5f8cc2fe6963586291a8eb59f62b9b8" "q-50222/selection/f2bba68d882be7460056eb5912844719ada485c852eee90d04d7481a6bdf5ffc" "q-50222/selection/c8d82fdc73de0541a9c808403f76f7917b4b2dd9eff2e49dd7c7822a871dd384" "q-50222/selection/58e3c9399a29c5a879685076ec2d3300653449b0f341bd390570fbd0f6a03961"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-50222" :question/id #uuid "f83185ca-7204-529d-8697-1b2d513b1e26" :question/math-academy-id "q-50222" :question/problem "$\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2})(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-50222/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2a41ede-381e-55f6-99e5-1baf1ea348a1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-50222"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352007/field-1/20d32cf233799bea8a56b69423239a5c4f10625f579bfbc44be980849d7664ee" :answer/id #uuid "eb0ddba6-3b2d-59e4-b606-d8ce04906c92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\pi-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352007/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "be2ee210-c00f-51bd-9f03-95a42879e609" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352007/field-1/20d32cf233799bea8a56b69423239a5c4f10625f579bfbc44be980849d7664ee" :answer-field/choices ["q-352007/field-1/20d32cf233799bea8a56b69423239a5c4f10625f579bfbc44be980849d7664ee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352007" :question/id #uuid "aff04484-af55-5b28-a67b-6ba87b372ad0" :question/math-academy-id "q-352007" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=5{x}^{2}+6\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=10x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(5{x}^{2}+6)(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(10x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,dx \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+D) \\\\  & =-(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=10D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-(5{x}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+10x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =(-(5{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+6)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}+10(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2})-(-6\\operatorname{cos}⁡0+10(0)\\operatorname{sin}⁡0+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =(0+5\\pi +0)-(-6+10) \\\\  & =5\\pi -4 \\\\  & =5\\pi -4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352007/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d2a41ede-381e-55f6-99e5-1baf1ea348a1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352007"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114942/selection/c47e170f61533c3333448510e37d8d0554bb4ab30bd5a6234c055daf984cce68" :answer/id #uuid "f88adea0-d279-58f8-bdd6-6d0f7508fe69" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{e}^{3}-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114942/selection/edb4c3967f7452daa9f1f263e045a2155ad4ae38efb3aa0aaaaa346a8e2a9a99" :answer/id #uuid "30781d14-b6c0-5a58-824d-a81f29c14f75" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114942/selection/0d32286068b9ddcc66b177519c49bb2af14200daa48601d0ac50f87e42e74ce0" :answer/id #uuid "aa2f8eab-ddbf-53ff-aea2-cee07cef01a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{3}-1}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114942/selection/35d0f3f620bf926203b3380d117362265b033998a0176dfbc71255e43b3b1834" :answer/id #uuid "362841d9-bd94-5733-b5b4-3ebaf864bdce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{2}-3}{4{ln}^{2}⁡2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114942/selection/8febe7e08572b620195c44ddd1f60058249db506e0315ff2b685cf82df7b7ea6" :answer/id #uuid "708690a8-3904-5a18-9c67-b4170cb121ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{2}+3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114942/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "77d20b7b-5118-5e02-b0e4-507965d171a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114942/selection/edb4c3967f7452daa9f1f263e045a2155ad4ae38efb3aa0aaaaa346a8e2a9a99" :answer-field/choices ["q-114942/selection/c47e170f61533c3333448510e37d8d0554bb4ab30bd5a6234c055daf984cce68" "q-114942/selection/edb4c3967f7452daa9f1f263e045a2155ad4ae38efb3aa0aaaaa346a8e2a9a99" "q-114942/selection/0d32286068b9ddcc66b177519c49bb2af14200daa48601d0ac50f87e42e74ce0" "q-114942/selection/35d0f3f620bf926203b3380d117362265b033998a0176dfbc71255e43b3b1834" "q-114942/selection/8febe7e08572b620195c44ddd1f60058249db506e0315ff2b685cf82df7b7ea6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114942" :question/id #uuid "5641ce86-0253-50e7-88d6-84e3602245b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-114942" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=9{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 9{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=3{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}(3{x}^{3})-\\int (3{x}^{3})(\\frac{2{log}_{2}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{2}⁡x\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}{log}_{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{2}⁡x)(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}(\\frac{{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+D) \\\\  & =3{x}^{3}{({log}_{2}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}{log}_{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{3}{ln}^{2}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\frac{2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}+\\frac{2{x}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{3})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{6D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{2}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.$\n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}9{x}^{2}({log}_{2}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{{x}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡x-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{3})]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡e-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+\\frac{2}{3})-\\frac{{1}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3{ln}^{2}⁡1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(3-2+\\frac{2}{3})-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡2}(0-0+\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3}}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}-\\frac{2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3{ln}^{2}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114942/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98a67346-c2c9-5d22-8adf-479fea81eaa2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114942"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114883/selection/f4281c5ea245222e04ff17c877e6722d7f6cd107e3bd93902a78c38cd51072e9" :answer/id #uuid "16db57ea-46d1-5ed9-983b-b2c7b2502046" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3e+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114883/selection/65a68d86761e51f6aae56f5841fe942840678204a7ff8c795a734519bda045b1" :answer/id #uuid "6a44baed-a7e5-5032-b4b4-c6829291dbde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "e-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114883/selection/850d7a49d893c15d16f7d32fa0c47cda9e4fcd9ea19fd7c75021c3be1b182798" :answer/id #uuid "c0653ac4-f75a-5eab-ae07-4af594193552" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3e-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114883/selection/7e8a480584c876ad06c513acf547b0aae542d71762fe13f8504917e837512d3b" :answer/id #uuid "5ae6ee1a-42b0-54cb-a84e-1e347005492b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9e-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114883/selection/9cf15c4b179abd844fa4f725fa2421b38d13648b1ae93474870e7ec66de20e2d" :answer/id #uuid "3ecc34da-5efd-5a64-8c0b-2ca48ca5f483" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9e+12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114883/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "90ffe1fc-a5d7-5cf0-94e3-5666d21a9bd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114883/selection/7e8a480584c876ad06c513acf547b0aae542d71762fe13f8504917e837512d3b" :answer-field/choices ["q-114883/selection/f4281c5ea245222e04ff17c877e6722d7f6cd107e3bd93902a78c38cd51072e9" "q-114883/selection/65a68d86761e51f6aae56f5841fe942840678204a7ff8c795a734519bda045b1" "q-114883/selection/850d7a49d893c15d16f7d32fa0c47cda9e4fcd9ea19fd7c75021c3be1b182798" "q-114883/selection/7e8a480584c876ad06c513acf547b0aae542d71762fe13f8504917e837512d3b" "q-114883/selection/9cf15c4b179abd844fa4f725fa2421b38d13648b1ae93474870e7ec66de20e2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114883" :question/id #uuid "eb91f706-c1af-5e21-8b85-187abaa8e83e" :question/math-academy-id "q-114883" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3}))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{6\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3}))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{3}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3\\int \\text{d}x \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})-3x+D) \\\\  & =x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+18x+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-6D.$ \n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x & ={[x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{3})-6x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})+18x]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =[e{ln}^{2}⁡({e}^{3})-6e\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})+18e]-[(1){ln}^{2}⁡({1}^{3})-6(1)\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{3})+18(1)] \\\\  & =9e-18e+18e-18 \\\\  & =9e-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114883/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98a67346-c2c9-5d22-8adf-479fea81eaa2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114883"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-114944/selection/ec1dec8022764419683a5bb54e98306117cf99f715950ebf63c96d6a0c8da123" :answer/id #uuid "492ba6a0-7957-55b4-bfde-c2271674cce6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{e}^{2}-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114944/selection/15cf9d53ad96bfe7442c327b93f98ce6df86cf3a284239c0c0da7e99aebe7fa0" :answer/id #uuid "a8ed13e5-ce22-5c99-bdba-262fe00eef2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4e+3}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114944/selection/06f37511c63fbf68bb20b8403b004e627c1e477588903c8bb011adbd632f6a5b" :answer/id #uuid "b0220c19-f45b-539d-832b-8ddce9dd86ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4e-8}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114944/selection/0517abda6b914bc04e891d2b0d0b115a551a6a2ebb24a7438d9be072576045d6" :answer/id #uuid "d3d8ba85-17ac-50cc-988b-c1a761c1bb17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{e}^{2}+6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114944/selection/3d2c4785a5654fa47b3ae50047841167b77d057ec4a39fed46c17b7a0f1ad3b7" :answer/id #uuid "b0a80d4b-2ce8-5e12-940d-a6f544e19d62" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{e-6}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-114944/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f003c01f-efca-50ce-b097-fd7c6186a30d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-114944/selection/06f37511c63fbf68bb20b8403b004e627c1e477588903c8bb011adbd632f6a5b" :answer-field/choices ["q-114944/selection/ec1dec8022764419683a5bb54e98306117cf99f715950ebf63c96d6a0c8da123" "q-114944/selection/15cf9d53ad96bfe7442c327b93f98ce6df86cf3a284239c0c0da7e99aebe7fa0" "q-114944/selection/06f37511c63fbf68bb20b8403b004e627c1e477588903c8bb011adbd632f6a5b" "q-114944/selection/0517abda6b914bc04e891d2b0d0b115a551a6a2ebb24a7438d9be072576045d6" "q-114944/selection/3d2c4785a5654fa47b3ae50047841167b77d057ec4a39fed46c17b7a0f1ad3b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-114944" :question/id #uuid "ef6393b1-d04e-5306-b659-0f27835e1bb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-114944" :question/problem "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\int (x)(\\frac{4{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})-\\frac{2x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D) \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}-\\frac{4x{log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2})}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{8x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x{ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{4x\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+\\frac{8x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+8)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{4D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nNote that in the above calculation we used the change of base formula ${log}_{3}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$\n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}{({log}_{3}⁡({x}^{2}))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={[\\frac{x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({x}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+8)]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({e}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{2})+8)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}({ln}^{2}⁡({1}^{2})-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({1}^{2})+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{e}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(4-8+8)-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}(0-0+8) \\\\  & =\\frac{4e-8}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-114944/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98a67346-c2c9-5d22-8adf-479fea81eaa2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-114944"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-352049/field-1/da8c1f1ce31d500eabc11c1c129757a966265457448f3e099a1859b5131e6515" :answer/id #uuid "3aa41091-0ab2-5f4e-ad39-e11086965817" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5e^3-2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-352049/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2110f93c-9dc8-5850-8e88-a44f5f8650af" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-352049/field-1/da8c1f1ce31d500eabc11c1c129757a966265457448f3e099a1859b5131e6515" :answer-field/choices ["q-352049/field-1/da8c1f1ce31d500eabc11c1c129757a966265457448f3e099a1859b5131e6515"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-352049" :question/id #uuid "a1ddafc6-2561-5d34-8429-bede58c8f919" :question/math-academy-id "q-352049" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1/3}^{e/3}243{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))^{2} & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=243{x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int 243{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=81{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 243{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}(81{x}^{3})-\\int (81{x}^{3})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =81{x}^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}-162\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x) & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 243{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =81{x}^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}-162\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =81{x}^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}-162(\\frac{{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}+D) \\\\  & =81{x}^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}-54{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+18{x}^{3}-162D \\\\  & ={x}^{3}(81{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}-54\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+18)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-162D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1/3}^{e/3}243{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))^{2}\\text{d}x & ={[{x}^{3}(81{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x))}^{2}-54\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3x)+18)]}_{1/3}^{e/3} \\\\  & =[{(\\frac{e}{3})}^{3}(81{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{e}{3}))}^{2}-54\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{e}{3})+18)] \\\\  & \\,-[{(\\frac{1}{3})}^{3}(81{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}))}^{2}-54\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3})+18)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{{e}^{3}}{27}(81{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)}^{2}-54\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+18)]-[\\frac{1}{27}(81{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)}^{2}-54\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+18)] \\\\  & =[\\frac{{e}^{3}}{27}(81-54+18)]-\\frac{1}{27}\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =\\frac{5{e}^{3}-2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-352049/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98a67346-c2c9-5d22-8adf-479fea81eaa2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-352049"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-12708/selection/bd13a9aa3efba35ff157cf619a1ccc0d5b60ea71a412d4b44fd8ac37d7d19bf8" :answer/id #uuid "6aa58726-c13b-5add-834b-ac023e4a62ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{3{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{3}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12708/selection/ce1ae3c2855cac290b87fbde7be18513f3667807c5c21f142101c736fdc7e4e8" :answer/id #uuid "68ec665d-5383-56a5-8aec-69399e614220" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12708/selection/8f5b617cb9b6a9e7a67c9793e4a2038772336da03933daa4b28ca6e1d15b7cda" :answer/id #uuid "2cea4065-d7d7-58a4-a77e-122972c73e74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{1}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12708/selection/831b9be1518847e3955685937748f145d16d271ec49d57a8ce1cb62588a6f658" :answer/id #uuid "04d9df7e-0377-57d5-8cae-d60a0dc50cdb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}+\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12708/selection/51689b9e7f01761dc555984961e3a0913624218a76cf280fd0070e131a3a6688" :answer/id #uuid "1f53230a-ac18-5819-b7aa-8fc4cd6a24fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x(3{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}+\\frac{{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-12708/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "044cf0d4-63f0-5c69-ba32-5a850ebc7d7e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-12708/selection/ce1ae3c2855cac290b87fbde7be18513f3667807c5c21f142101c736fdc7e4e8" :answer-field/choices ["q-12708/selection/bd13a9aa3efba35ff157cf619a1ccc0d5b60ea71a412d4b44fd8ac37d7d19bf8" "q-12708/selection/ce1ae3c2855cac290b87fbde7be18513f3667807c5c21f142101c736fdc7e4e8" "q-12708/selection/8f5b617cb9b6a9e7a67c9793e4a2038772336da03933daa4b28ca6e1d15b7cda" "q-12708/selection/831b9be1518847e3955685937748f145d16d271ec49d57a8ce1cb62588a6f658" "q-12708/selection/51689b9e7f01761dc555984961e3a0913624218a76cf280fd0070e131a3a6688"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-12708" :question/id #uuid "35c6bb4e-1ad8-5bd0-8b19-4423d0943b19" :question/math-academy-id "q-12708" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡x}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate  $\\int {log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={log}_{3}⁡(x)\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\,\\text{d}x=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {log}_{3}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({log}_{3}⁡(x))(x)-\\int (x)(\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant.\n\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({log}_{3}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =x{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x{log}_{3}⁡(x)-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+D) \\\\  & =x{({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2x{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2x}{{ln}^{2}⁡3}-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =x({({log}_{3}⁡x)}^{2}-\\frac{2{log}_{3}⁡(x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+\\frac{2}{{ln}^{2}⁡3})+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-\\frac{2D}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-12708/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "98a67346-c2c9-5d22-8adf-479fea81eaa2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-12708"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7053"] :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_0^1 (t^2+1)e^{2t+1} \\, \\textrm{d} t.$" :question/worked-solution "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={t}^{2}+1\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2t, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{2t+1}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =({t}^{2}+1)(\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{2})(2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}}{2}-\\int t\\,{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int t\\,e^{2t+1}\\,\\textrm{d}t.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=1 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}={e}^{2t+1}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int t\\,{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t)(\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{2})-\\int (\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{2})(1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{t\\,{e}^{2t+1}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{t\\,{e}^{2t+1}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{4}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}}{2}-\\int t\\,{e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}}{2}-(\\frac{t\\,{e}^{2t+1}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{4}+D) \\\\  & =\\frac{({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}}{2}-\\frac{t\\,{e}^{2t+1}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{4}-D \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{4}(2{t}^{2}-2t+3)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C = -{D}.$ \n\nFinally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+1){e}^{2t+1}\\,\\text{d}t & ={[\\frac{{e}^{2t+1}}{4}(2{t}^{2}-2t+3)]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{e}^{2(1)+1}}{4}(2(1)^{2}-2(1)+3))-(\\frac{{e}^{2(0)+1}}{4}(2(0)^{2}-2(0)+3)) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{3}}{4}(2-2+3)-\\frac{e}{4}(0-0+3) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{e}^{3}}{4}-\\frac{3e}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{e}^{3}-3e}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-495"] :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int x^2\\cos(3x) \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2x\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =({x}^{2})(\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))-\\int (\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int x\\sin(3x) \\textrm{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x=-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))-\\int (-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x))+{C}_{1} \\\\  & =-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{9}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+{C}_{1}\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1$ is a constant of integration.\nSo we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{2}{3}\\int x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{2}{3}(-\\,\\frac{1}{3}\\,x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{9}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+{C}_{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{2}{9}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-\\frac{2}{27}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-\\frac{2{C}_{1}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{27}((9{x}^{2}-2)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+6x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C = -\\dfrac{2C_1}{3}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-496"] :question/problem "Evaluate the integral $\\displaystyle \\int_1^e 32x^3(\\ln x)^2 \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2} & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=32{x}^{3} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 32{x}^{3}\\text{d}x=8{x}^{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 32{x}^{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}(8{x}^{4})-\\int (8{x}^{4})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{x}^{4}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-16\\int {x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int {x^3\\ln(x)} \\textrm{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x) & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{3} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{3}\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4})(\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\int {x}^{3}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{16}+{C}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1$ is an integral constant. So, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 32{x}^{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =8{x}^{4}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-16\\int {x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{x}^{4}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-16(\\frac{{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{16}+{C}_{1}) \\\\  & =8{x}^{4}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-4{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+{x}^{4}-16{C}_{1} \\\\  & ={x}^{4}(8{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1)+C\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C = -4C_1.$ Finally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}32{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\text{d}x & ={{x}^{4}(8{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1)|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =[(e)^{4}(8{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e))}^{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(e)+1)]-[(1)^{4}(8{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1))}^{2}-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)+1)] \\\\  & =[{e}^{4}(8-4+1)]-1 \\\\  & =5{e}^{4}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
